  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Find the Network",
      "desc": "A beacon, then a probe",
      "detail": "About ten times a second the router’s Wi-Fi sends a beacon: here is \"HomeNet\", protected with WPA2, on channel 36. The laptop could simply wait to hear one; to be quicker it also asks out loud with a probe request, and the access point answers with a probe response.",
