    {
      "title": "Encrypted Now",
      "desc": "And what a listener could still do",
      "detail": "Every data frame is encrypted now, like this first one carrying a DHCP Discover: anyone nearby sees only the MAC addresses and the size. But someone who recorded the four handshake messages can try password guesses at home, as fast as their computer allows: a guess is right when it gives the same MIC. A long, random password makes that hopeless; WPA3 removes the weakness.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Others see",
          "MAC addresses, sizes, timing"
        ],
        [
          "Weak point",
          "Offline password guessing"
        ],
        [
          "Defence",
          "A long password, or WPA3"
        ]
      ],
